[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"669","stub":{"id":"669","section":"U.S. 60 to Firetower Rd. (6.3 miles)","altname":"","river":"Otter Creek (Ohio trib.)","difficulty":"II","states":["USA-KEN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112523","location":{"latitude":"37.8996658325195","longitude":"-86.0253067016602"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117810","location":{"latitude":"37.9594573974609","longitude":"-86.0538711547852"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"6.3","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"15412","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9318","description":"First there is a small drop with a little white water, and then the whole creek washes up on this undercut bank. It is undercut by at least 10 feet and would pose a threat to any tipped kayaker I would think. ","caption":"Undercut Bank","poi_name":"Little rapid followed by an undercut bank","subject":"Undercut Bank","author":"Chris","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/15412","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/15412"}},{"id":"16135","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9317","description":"This is the boof on the left side of the creek at the put-in/park and surf. At 500 CFS it's a scrape, and 700 CFS is much better. At 1300 - 2000 CFS there is a nice sticky hole behind it that we like to surf in, and I even flipped 3 times that day, and hit my head once. We normally ALWAYS where are PFD's, but we forgot when we went to take these pictures, because we got distracted.","caption":"Park and Surf Boof","poi_name":"Park and Surf Boof","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16135","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16135"}},{"id":"15410","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9318","description":"My brother acctually crashed right through this rapid in his raft, but I'm sure a kayaker can surf it because I have done it in my raft a few times. At 500 CFS the wave splits, and I was even able to surf from one side to the other catching the other half of the wave. At 700 CFS it's great, and me and my brother thought it washed out a bit when it was at 900 CFS. This is the best rapid I have seen on this creek, but I haven't been all the way down it yet.","caption":"The puttin park and surf rapid","poi_name":"The puttin park and surf rapid ? that's what I call it ?","subject":"My brother Tim","author":"Chris","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/15410","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/15410"}},{"id":"40832","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9312","description":"A frown shaped hole that flushes out on the left. The middle of course was the biggest part like it always is with a frown. You could escape it while surfing with some effort.","caption":"Surf City at 2950 CFS","poi_name":"Surf City","subject":"Surfcity","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40832","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40832"}},{"id":"40834","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9312","description":"","caption":"Elkhorn Creek Sunset","poi_name":"","subject":"Elkhorn Creek Sunset","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40834","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40834"}},{"id":"40836","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9312","description":"","caption":"Otter Creek at 1900 CFS","poi_name":"put in rapid","subject":"Chris on the put in rapid","author":"Tim","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/40836","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/40836"}},{"id":"15411","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9318","description":"This part is right before blue hole, and right at the end of it there is a ledge that's only on the right side, so don't miss it.","caption":"Blue Hole","poi_name":"Blue Hole's Half Ledge ? how about that ?","subject":"Blue Hole","author":"Chris","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/15411","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/15411"}},{"id":"15409","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9317","description":"You can't acctually drive up close to blue hole, it is a little ways of a hike up that cedar hill to where I normally park. I think if you go all the way to the end; you have to go down the ohio for a minute to get to the boat ramp(where parking is), but you could hike out Otter Creek Trail, but it would be quite a long walk I bet.","caption":"Otter Creek Trail Map","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/15409","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/15409"}}],"detail":{"id":"669","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"For more information, see the \"comments\" tab.","averageGradient":"12","maxGradient":"0","length":"9.7","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112523","117810"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-86.02525406631075,37.8998328912538],[-86.02506717691222,37.89977400783869],[-86.02506171024555,37.89977220783868],[-86.02442211024652,37.89973507450537],[-86.02405951024707,37.89977427450532],[-86.02389391024735,37.89983347450527],[-86.02370411024765,37.90011220783816],[-86.02386301337242,37.9007010151289],[-86.02387997691403,37.90076387450381],[-86.02422291024688,37.90113800783655],[-86.024869910